    ["The decision","JUDGE","Stable OCV is one release indicator, not proof of a defect-free cell. Excessive voltage loss can indicate elevated self-discharge, leakage or an internal defect and should trigger the manufacturer’s investigation and rejection criteria."]],
  params:["State of charge at the start of aging: 30–80%","Aging time: up to 3 weeks","Room temperature: approximately 20–25 °C","High temperature: approximately 30–50 °C"],
  alts:["Sequence and duration of HT and NT aging vary by manufacturer and chemistry"],
  innov:["Measurement technology for early quality detection"],
  qInf:["Orientation of cells","Packing density of the cell good carriers","Ambient temperature"],
  qFeat:["Capacity","Internal resistance","Self-discharge rate"],
  sop:["Set the starting SOC","Load HT racks and log the start OCV","Transfer to NT aging on schedule","Measure OCV at each interval","Flag any cell drifting beyond the limit","Release only cells with stable OCV"] },

{ id:"eol", no:"15", phase:"Cell finishing", title:"End-of-line testing", machine:"eol", routes:ALL,
  env:{iso:"—", dew:"—", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 5–15 M (EoL test)", takt:"—",
  purpose:"Measure what each cell actually is, sort it, and ship it at a safe state of charge.",
  inp:"Aged cell", out:"Graded, packed cell",
  parts:[
    ["EOL test rig","TEST","Cells undergo a defined capacity test with specified charge, rest, discharge and cutoff conditions. The cell is then adjusted to its shipping SOC; pulse, DC-resistance, optical, OCV and leakage tests vary by manufacturer."],
    ["Grading","SORT","Many manufacturers sort cells into classes by performance data, so that cells built into one pack are matched. Listed as an optional process."],
